asking ye shall receive  into the dalek if you saw my review of  deep breath wish was peter capaldi's  first episode  full episode at any rate as the new  doctor  well you may recall i said i was liking  what he was doing but he didn't  have me totally hooked into me and i was  waiting for you know those sort of  moments where i'm like  yeah that's the doctor well you know  what i got them pretty much  out of the gate on this episode the  pre-credit stuff just  the way he's interacting with the  characters that he's meeting for the  very first time and this  general dismissiveness he sort of has  and you can tell he's  he cares but the man's got no time for  niceties anymore  and i feel like in just a couple of  scenes i  got his doctor i buy into it i'm like  this  is the doctor this is i'm down with this  let's go  and it goes it goes very well i think  the moment  that it finally sold me on and out i  feel okay talking about this because  like i said i try to avoid spoilers but  this is  literally the first three minutes of the  episode but there's a woman a soldier  on the tardis pointing a gun at him  demanding that he  take her to her command carrier and he  keeps cutting her off and  telling her no and that she's saying it  wrong and he  keeps doing that until she asks politely  and says please  and then he takes her and he does it  with this so and this is not a game he's  being dead serious he's not playing  around it's not a test he  he's not going to do it till she asks  him nicely and  he sells that you know there's a cert  there's an arrogance there's a pomposity  to that  that really could have gone the wrong  way if you  had an actor that was pulling that kind  of stuff  but just didn't have the charisma that  peter capaldi has  it it wouldn't work but it works so i am  definitely down with a new guy how's the  episode  it's pretty darn good i love the daleks  naturally  and this is the daleks from a different  perspective  quite literally in fact but the doctor  and clara and a couple of soldiers they  get  physically trunking down and they go  inside a dalek  now as hokey and gimmicky as that sounds  it it  really does work because the reason that  they're going in is very compelling what  they're trying to accomplish once  they're there is really interesting  clara's working for me a little bit more  in this episode i still i still can't  get completely on board with her but  she's definitely working better for me  than she did last time because last time  she was all weird about  the doctor's regeneration even before he  was  showing the aspect of his new  personality which just didn't make any  sense to me given that she knew what  regeneration was  but now that she's seeing all these  sides of his personality and aspects to  him that she hadn't seen before that she  now has to cope with  now it makes a little bit more sense the  way that her interactions with him  are changing and how she's trying to  kind of deal with that  but she's also just rolling with it  better in general so it's a much better  balance than she had going on last time  around  we get the introduction of a character  called danny pink who it's been  mentioned  may serve as some sort of pseudo  additional companion it's it's been a  little vague maybe it's been made more  clear i try not to dig too much into  this stuff because i'd like to avoid  spoilers if i can  but i know he's going to be a recurring  character and we don't see him a ton but  i like him right off the bat he is fun  he's funny he's layered he's a soldier  which is really interesting because  the show has always taken pretty much  the doctor's perspective on soldiers and  the doctor does not have a great deal of  respect or  interest in soldiers he doesn't like  people who just follow orders and he  doesn't like people with a military  mentality and the show is pretty much  sided with him across the board on that  whenever soldiers or military characters  have shown 